5. Runtime Polymorphism (Most Important Topic)
Definition
  Method call is resolved at runtime based on object type, not reference type.

Achieved using:
  Inheritance (or interface)
  Method overriding
  Parent reference & child object

Example
class Parent {
    void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent method");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    @Override
    void show() {
        System.out.println("Child method");
    }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Parent p = new Child();
        p.show();
    }
}

Output
Child method

👉 Key Rule (Say in interview)

Reference decides accessibility, object decides behavior.


6. Conditions for Runtime Polymorphism
  ✔ IS-A relationship (inheritance / interface)
  ✔ Method overriding
  ✔ Parent reference
  ✔ Child object
  ❌ static methods
  ❌ final methods
  ❌ private methods

7. How Runtime Polymorphism Works (JVM Internals 🔥)
    Compiler checks method existence using reference type
    JVM resolves method call using actual object
    Uses Dynamic Method Dispatch
    Internally uses Virtual Method Table (V-Table)
👉 That’s why overridden methods are called at runtime.

8. Method Overriding Rules (Very Important)
| Rule             | Explanation              |
| ---------------- | ------------------------ |
| Method signature | Must be same             |
| Access modifier  | Cannot reduce visibility |
| Return type      | Covariant allowed        |
| static           | Cannot override          |
| final            | Cannot override          |
| private          | Not inherited            |

Covariant Return Type:
  class Parent {
      Number getValue() {
          return 10;
      }
  }
  
  class Child extends Parent {
      Integer getValue() {
          return 20;
      }
  }
  
  public class Test {
      public static void main(String[] args) {
          Parent p = new Child();
          System.out.println(p.getValue());
      }
  }
  
  Output
  20

9. Static Methods & Polymorphism (Tricky 🔥)
class Parent {
    static void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent static");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    static void show() {
        System.out.println("Child static");
    }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Parent p = new Child();
        p.show();
    }
}

Output
Parent static

👉 This is method hiding, NOT polymorphism
👉 Static binding happens at compile time

10. Polymorphism Using Interfaces (Very Important)
Example
interface Payment {
    void pay();
}

class CreditCardPayment implements Payment {
    public void pay() {
        System.out.println("Credit Card Payment");
    }
}

class UpiPayment implements Payment {
    public void pay() {
        System.out.println("UPI Payment");
    }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Payment p = new UpiPayment();
        p.pay();
    }
}

Output
UPI Payment

✔ Most common real-world polymorphism
✔ Core of Spring DI

13. Polymorphism in Spring Boot (🔥 Extremely Important)
Dependency Injection Example:
@Service
class OrderService {

    private final Payment payment;

    public OrderService(Payment payment) {
        this.payment = payment;
    }
}

At runtime:
  Spring injects actual implementation
  Behavior changes without code modification

Multiple Implementations
  @Qualifier("upiPayment")
